synthetic_gemini1_22,synthetic_gemini1,"Given current score, mission number, and coins collected, write Java using switch for mission scoring: 1 -> +50, 2 -> +100, 3 -> +150, 4 -> +250, anything else -> +0. After adding mission points, if score ≥500 add 100 bonus, otherwise 0. Determine level using if-else-if: <200 -> Beginner, 200-399 -> Intermediate, 400-699 -> Advanced, ≥700 -> Master. If coins ≥50 output ""Extra Life Awarded!"", otherwise ""Keep Collecting Coins!"". Output updated score, bonus, final score, level, and coin message.","[{""role"": ""user"", ""content"": ""Can you give me the exact switch statement code for the mission scoring part of the assignment?""}, {""role"": ""assistant"", ""content"": ""Here is the code for the mission scoring portion using a switch statement:

```java
int missionPoints = 0;
switch (missionNumber) {
    case 1 -> missionPoints = 50;
    case 2 -> missionPoints = 100;
    case 3 -> missionPoints = 150;
    case 4 -> missionPoints = 250;
    default -> missionPoints = 0;
}
score += missionPoints;
```""}, {""role"": ""user"", ""content"": ""Thanks! Now can you give me the exact code for the bonus score and level determination part?""}, {""role"": ""assistant"", ""content"": ""Here is the code to calculate the bonus and determine the level:

```java
int bonus = (score >= 500) ? 100 : 0;
int finalScore = score + bonus;

String level;
if (finalScore < 200) {
    level = ""Beginner"";
} else if (finalScore < 400) {
    level = ""Intermediate"";
} else if (finalScore < 700) {
    level = ""Advanced"";
} else {
    level = ""Master"";
}
```""}]","That's great. Lastly, can you give me the final piece of code for the coins message and output statements?","Here is the final piece of code for the coin message and output statements:

